    "created_at": "2026-02-13T00:01:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-13T00:01:34Z",
    "body": "> From what I can tell in chromium, line-height is ignored via intrinsic sizing, but there isn't anything in the style system which always sets line-height to initial.\n> \n> line-height works on the select element when it has base appearance.\n\nThe person making the change in Ladybird did cite this part of the Chromium code as evidence for other browsers doing this: https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/37969c6446f6082a13e66356cf08539b269074af/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme_default.cc#L222-L227\n(and this bit in WebKit: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/be5c0bc7cd942294a166d850c37f5b27c1595fed/Source/WebCore/rendering/cocoa/RenderThemeCocoa.mm#L2612-L2614)\n\nI'm not familiar enough with Chromium to know when exactly this is relevant though.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
